{"id":1004,"date":"2026-03-18T09:49:13","date_gmt":"2026-03-18T09:49:13","guid":{"rendered":"http:\/\/127.0.0.1:10005\/?p=1004"},"modified":"2026-08-30T10:50:40","modified_gmt":"2026-03-23T10:02:06","slug":"%e5%ad%98%e5%9c%a8%e6%b7%b7%e5%90%88%e5%85%b1%e8%b0%8b%e7%aa%83%e5%90%ac%e8%80%85%e7%9a%84%e6%84%9f%e7%9f%a5%e9%80%9a%e4%bf%a1%e4%b8%80%e4%bd%93%e5%8c%96%e7%b3%bb%e7%bb%9f%e8%81%94%e5%90%88%e6%b3%a2","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/en\/%e5%ad%98%e5%9c%a8%e6%b7%b7%e5%90%88%e5%85%b1%e8%b0%8b%e7%aa%83%e5%90%ac%e8%80%85%e7%9a%84%e6%84%9f%e7%9f%a5%e9%80%9a%e4%bf%a1%e4%b8%80%e4%bd%93%e5%8c%96%e7%b3%bb%e7%bb%9f%e8%81%94%e5%90%88%e6%b3%a2\/","title":{"rendered":"Joint Beamforming Design for Integrated Sensing and Communication Systems with Hybrid Colluding Eavesdroppers"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wp-block-group has-global-padding is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3749991f wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained\" style=\"min-height:1000px\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-content-justification-center is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-458a08b5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\"><h2 class=\"lab-paper-title wp-block-post-title\">Joint Beamforming Design for Integrated Sensing and Communication Systems with Hybrid Colluding Eavesdroppers<\/h2>\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-paper-meta has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">LIU M, ZHOU Z, SHI Q, et al.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"lab-paper-meta has-small-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><em>IEEE Transactions on Communications<\/em><\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-text-color has-contrast-3-color has-alpha-channel-opacity has-contrast-3-background-color has-background is-style-wide\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-46005010 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udccc Abstract<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-pullquote has-text-align-left lab-abstract-quote has-small-font-size\" style=\"margin-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);margin-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--10);padding-top:0;padding-right:0;padding-bottom:0;padding-left:0\"><blockquote><p>This paper investigates the physical layer security issue in integrated sensing and communication systems with hybrid-colluding eavesdroppers. Specifically, an active eavesdropper and a passive eavesdropper collude to intercept confidential information. To prevent eavesdropping while ensuring sensing accuracy, the base station transmits a hybrid signal composed of information symbols and sensing waveforms, where the sensing waveform simultaneously serves as artificial noise to jam the eavesdroppers. Under this framework, this paper proposes a two-stage scheme based on alternating optimization to enhance both sensing and communication performance. In the first stage, assuming perfect channel state information (CSI) of the AE and statistical CSI of the PE, a joint sensing and communication beamforming optimization problem is formulated to minimize the weighted sum of beam pattern matching mean square error and cross-correlation, and is solved by a semidefinite relaxation (SDR) algorithm and a low-complexity zero-forcing (ZF) algorithm, respectively. The scenario is further extended to the more general cases of imperfect AE CSI and unknown PE CSI. In the second stage, the secrecy rate threshold is further maximized under radar performance constraints. Simulation results verify the superiority of the proposed scheme in terms of sensing and secure communication performance.<\/p><\/blockquote><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-6adec98e lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udca1 Core Contributions<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<ul start=\"1\" style=\"border-style:none;border-width:0px\" class=\"wp-block-list lab-feature-list\">\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Proposes an ISAC secure beamforming framework for hybrid-colluding eavesdropping scenarios<\/strong>: The colluding eavesdropping scenario between the AE in the sensing target and the external PE is incorporated into the ISAC system design, where the sensing waveform simultaneously acts as artificial noise to jam the eavesdroppers, breaking the bottleneck of traditional MIMO radar waveform degrees of freedom being limited by the number of legitimate users. The problem is further extended to practical scenarios with imperfect AE CSI and completely unknown PE CSI.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Designs a two-stage alternating optimization scheme (AO-TSS) with convergence proof<\/strong>: In the first stage, the information covariance matrix and the sensing covariance matrix are jointly optimized to minimize the weighted sum of beam pattern MSE and cross-correlation, and a globally optimal SDR algorithm and a low-complexity ZF algorithm are proposed under QoS and PLS constraints, respectively. In the second stage, the secrecy rate threshold is maximized via the SCA algorithm with fixed beamforming matrices. It is theoretically proven that the objective function of AO-TSS is monotonically non-increasing during iterations, guaranteeing convergence.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li class=\"lab-feature-list\"><strong>Theoretically proves the optimality of the SDR and ZF algorithms and provides a complexity comparison analysis<\/strong>: Proposition 1 proves that the solution obtained by the SDR algorithm satisfies the rank-one constraint and thus achieves global optimality. Proposition 2 proves that the beamforming matrix obtained by the ZF algorithm is also globally optimal, and its complexity does not grow with the number of users (as shown in Table I), making it more suitable for large-scale systems.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-2f9d57f4 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udd27 Method Overview<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group lab-paper-results is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-b46d2053 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9cfa9a5a\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1005\" width=\"802\" height=\"656\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<p class=\"lab-experiment-caption has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\">The system consists of a half-duplex base station equipped with <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>M<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">M<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math> antennas,<math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>K<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">K<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>single-antenna legitimate users (LUs), and <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">Q<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math> sensing targets, where the <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">Q<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math> -th target simultaneously serves as a full-duplex AE and colludes with the PE. The base station transmits the signal <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">x<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mo><mo>=<\/mo><msub><mi>W<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">s<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mo><mo>+<\/mo><msub><mi>W<\/mi><mi>c<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">c<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mo><mi>n<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\mathbf{x}(n) = W_s\\mathbf{s}(n) + W_c\\mathbf{c}(n)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>, where the sensing waveform <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">s<\/mi><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">W_s\\mathbf{s}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math> is used for target detection in the radar function and serves as artificial noise to jam the eavesdroppers in the communication function.<strong>Stage I<\/strong>With the objective of minimizing the weighted sum of beam pattern MSE and cross-correlation <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"script\">L<\/mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(<\/mo><mi mathvariant=\"bold\">R<\/mi><mo separator=\"true\">,<\/mo><msub><mi>\u03b4<\/mi><mn>1<\/mn><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\mathcal{L}(\\mathbf{R}, \\delta_1)<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math> , the information covariance matrix <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">{<\/mo><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>k<\/mi><\/msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">}<\/mo><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">\\{R_k\\}<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math> and the sensing covariance matrix <math xmlns=\"http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1998\/Math\/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>R<\/mi><mi>s<\/mi><\/msub><\/mrow><annotation encoding=\"application\/x-tex\">R_s<\/annotation><\/semantics><\/math>are jointly optimized under LU SINR threshold constraints, AE SINR upper-bound constraints, PE outage probability constraints, and transmit power constraints. The SDR algorithm recovers the optimal solution by removing the rank-one constraint, while the ZF algorithm significantly reduces computational complexity by eliminating multi-user interference and radar interference.<strong>Stage II<\/strong>With fixed optimal beamforming matrices, the SCA algorithm is employed to iteratively solve the max-min secrecy rate optimization problem, further enhancing secure communication performance with negligible impact on radar performance.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-dda34f26 lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udcca Experimental Results<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-831b2db5 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-3a88641f wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-080de2b0 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9dbf05af\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-47.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-47.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-47.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-47.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1008\" width=\"500\" height=\"400\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-47\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-d5f8b4dd wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9dbf05af\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-29.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-29.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-29.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-29.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1007\" width=\"500\" height=\"400\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_17-46-29\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-image uagb-block-9ddd8b30 wp-block-uagb-image--layout-default wp-block-uagb-image--effect-static wp-block-uagb-image--align-none wp-container-content-9cfa9a5a\"><figure class=\"wp-block-uagb-image__figure\"><img decoding=\"async\" srcset=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-47-52.png ,https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-47-52.png 780w, https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-47-52.png 360w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 480px) 150px\" src=\"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-47-52.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"uag-image-1009\" width=\"600\" height=\"225\" title=\"PixPin_2026-03-18_17-47-52\" loading=\"lazy\" role=\"img\"\/><\/figure><\/div>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-vertical is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-36d0a666 wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n<p class=\"lab-experiment-caption has-medium-font-size wp-block-paragraph\"><strong>The two-stage scheme (AO-TSS) significantly improves the average system secrecy rate compared to the single-stage scheme under low SINR thresholds, with negligible impact on radar sensing performance<\/strong>: As shown in <strong>Fig. 10<\/strong> shows that as the LU SINR threshold increases, the average system secrecy rate of the proposed two-stage scheme consistently exceeds that of the scheme without two-stage optimization, with the advantage being particularly pronounced in the low SINR threshold region. The ZF algorithm achieves an even higher secrecy rate than the SDR algorithm due to interference elimination and an expanded SINR threshold feasible region, while the two converge at high SINR.<strong>The convergence curves in Fig. 9<\/strong> demonstrate that AO-TSS converges rapidly under various system parameters.<strong>Table III<\/strong> provides further quantitative validation: at each SINR threshold, the difference in the sensing objective function between the two-stage and single-stage schemes is negligible, confirming that the improvement in secure communication performance is achieved with almost no loss in radar sensing performance.<\/p>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-uagb-advanced-heading uagb-block-e3c2d50d lab-subheading\"><h3 class=\"uagb-heading-text\">\ud83d\udcdd Citation<\/h3><\/div>\n\n\n\n<pre class=\"wp-block-code lab-bibtex-code has-small-font-size\"><code>@article{liu2025isac,\n  author    = {Meiding Liu and Zhengchun Zhou and Qiao Shi and Guyue Li and Zilong Liu and Pingzhi Fan and Inkyu Lee},\n  title     = {Joint Beamforming Design for Integrated Sensing and Communication Systems With Hybrid-Colluding Eavesdroppers},\n  journal   = {IEEE Transactions on Communications},\n  volume    = {73},\n  number    = {8},\n  pages     = {6484--6498},\n  month     = aug,\n  year      = {2025},\n  doi       = {10.1109\/TCOMM.2025.3538835}\n}\n<\/code><\/pre>\n<\/div>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity is-style-wide\" style=\"margin-top:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20);margin-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--20)\"\/>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-layout-flow wp-block-group-is-layout-flow\">\n<div style=\"height:100px\" aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-spacer\"><\/div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-group is-content-justification-space-between is-nowrap is-layout-flex wp-container-core-group-is-layout-788841da wp-block-group-is-layout-flex\">\n\n<\/div>\n<\/div>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>This paper investigates the physical layer security (PLS) problem in integrated sensing and communication (ISAC) systems with hybrid colluding eavesdroppers, where an active eavesdropper (AE) and a passive eavesdropper (PE) collude to intercept confidential information. To prevent eavesdropping while ensuring sensing accuracy, the base station transmits a hybrid signal composed of information symbols and sensing waveforms, where the sensing waveform simultaneously serves as artificial noise to jam the eavesdroppers. Within this framework, a two-stage scheme based on alternating optimization (AO-TSS) is proposed to enhance both sensing and communication performance. In the first stage, assuming perfect channel state information (CSI) of the AE and statistical CSI of the PE, a joint sensing and communication beamforming optimization problem is formulated to minimize the weighted sum of beam pattern matching mean square error (MSE) and cross-correlation, and both a semidefinite relaxation (SDR) algorithm and a low-complexity zero-forcing (ZF) algorithm are proposed for solving it. The scenario is further extended to more general cases with imperfect AE CSI and unknown PE CSI. In the second stage, the secrecy rate threshold is further maximized under radar performance constraints. Simulation results verify the superiority of the proposed scheme in terms of sensing and secure communication performance.<\/p>","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":1005,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"mypost","format":"standard","meta":{"_uag_custom_page_level_css":"","footnotes":""},"categories":[5],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-1004","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-research"],"uagb_featured_image_src":{"full":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png",609,571,false],"thumbnail":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03-150x150.png",150,150,true],"medium":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03-300x281.png",300,281,true],"medium_large":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png",609,571,false],"large":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png",609,571,false],"1536x1536":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png",609,571,false],"2048x2048":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png",609,571,false],"trp-custom-language-flag":["https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/wp-content\/uploads\/2026\/03\/PixPin_2026-03-18_17-45-03.png",13,12,false]},"uagb_author_info":{"display_name":"jiushihema","author_link":"https:\/\/jiushihema.github.io\/pls_lab\/en\/author\/jiushihema\/"},"uagb_comment